<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imre Thököly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1657">1657</a>–<a href="/years/1705">1705</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imre Thököly was a Hungarian Lutheran noble who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule from 1678. With Ottoman backing he ruled the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hungary">Upper Hungary</a> from 1682 and married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilona-zrinyi">Ilona Zrínyi</a>. After the Ottoman defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683 his state collapsed, and he died in exile in Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly.jpg" alt="Imre Thököly" width="296" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thokolyi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Imre Thököly was born in Késmárk, now Kežmarok in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, on 25 September 1657, the fifth son of Count István Thököly and the only one to survive childhood. His father was among the wealthiest nobles of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hungary">Upper Hungary</a>. He studied at the Lutheran lyceum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/presov">Eperjes</a> from 1668. In 1670 his father was accused of joining the aristocrats' conspiracy against Leopold I and died during the siege of Árva Castle on 4 December; accounts differ on how the son got away to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>.</p><p>His estates in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> were confiscated, but he kept his Transylvanian lands and continued his studies at the Reformed college of Nagyenyed. Meanwhile Leopold I appointed a Directorium in 1673 that pursued a violent anti-Protestant policy, and refugees, called kuruc, raided the borderlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-hungary">Royal Hungary</a>.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Career</h2><p>The princely council appointed him to command the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> army on 26 September 1677, after a treaty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> promised an annual subsidy. He joined the Kuruc at Derecske on 27 November. In 1678 he captured Szendrő and Murány and the mining towns of the Garam valley, and he kept control of thirteen counties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-hungary">Royal Hungary</a> after a defeat at Barsszentkereszt. Reinforced in 1681, he forced the emperor to grant an armistice. In June 1682 he married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilona-zrinyi">Ilona Zrínyi</a>, widow of Francis I Rákóczi.</p><p>Sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-iv">Mehmed IV</a> gave him the title King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hungary">Upper Hungary</a> on condition of an annual tribute of 40,000 thalers. He assisted the Turks at the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683, and the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> blamed him for the defeat. In 1685 he was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/presov">Prešov</a>, and the Turks seized him at Nagyvárad and sent him in chains to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Edirne</a>. Released in 1686, he was imprisoned a second time before the Turks sent him into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> in 1690. He won at Zărneşti and was elected prince of Transylvania, but left in 1691.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Thököly led the Turkish cavalry at Slankamen and distinguished himself at Zenta in 1697. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 26 January 1699 excluded him by name from its amnesty. After another failed attempt on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> in 1700 he settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galata">Galata</a> with his wife, holding estates from Sultan Mustafa II and the title of count of Widdin. He died in 1705 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izmit">İzmit</a> and is buried at Kežmarok. His statue stands on Heroes' Square in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a>, and a street and a memorial in İzmit commemorate him.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Emeric Thököly” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Revolts by Bocskai, <b>Thököly</b> and Rákóczi defended Protestant and noble rights; the Reform Era brought Széchenyi's modernisation.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1526-1867">Kingdom of Hungary (1526-1867)</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Imre Thököly</b>, a Lutheran noble, led the Kuruc rebels of northern Hungary against Habsburg persecution of Protestants from 1678.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-upper-hungary">Principality of Upper Hungary</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Kežmarok, in what is now <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izmit">İzmit</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=49.14,20.43&amp;year=1688" aria-label="Kežmarok on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Imre Thököly"><image href="/maps/globes/g030n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4467 5885h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4467 5885h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=49.14,20.43&amp;year=1688">What was here in 1688? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
